theHarvester on Parrot
=====================

Commands: theHarvester, theharvester (compatibility alias), restfulHarvest.
The REST API is not started automatically and defaults to loopback.

Configuration: /etc/theHarvester/api-keys.yaml and proxies.yaml. Files under
~/.theHarvester take precedence, following upstream's configuration lookup.
Wordlists and default configuration are included in the private package data.

The application and four unavailable/incompatible libraries are installed in
/usr/lib/theharvester/venv. The rest come from APT, including Python 3.13,
Node.js and Chromium. No virtualenv activation or pip installation is necessary.
Do not modify the package-managed venv using pip; use APT for package updates.

Screenshots use the system Chromium, not a browser downloaded by Playwright.
Both the CLI and REST API use the private environment automatically. Launchers
ignore PYTHONPATH and Python's user site to avoid accidental dependency mixing.

For version/provenance details see vendor-lock.json and runtime-versions.json
in this directory. Full bundled license notices are under vendor-licenses/.
